 Each `status` sets the step's icon, and an `error` step turns its accent bar red."},"792":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-25","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#not-started","content":"Omit `currentStep` for a flow that hasn't begun: every step is `future` and none is marked current."},"793":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-26","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#vertical","content":"Use `orientation=\"vertical\"` to place the accent bar on the leading edge and stack steps in a column."},"794":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-27","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#interactive","content":"Give a step an `onPress` handler to make it navigable. Steps without `onPress` are inert."},"795":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-28","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#disabled","content":"A disabled interactive step is muted, removed from the tab order, and cannot be activated."},"796":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-29","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#hide-step-numbers","content":"Step numbers are prepended automatically. Set `hideStepNumbers` to omit them."},"797":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-30","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#customization","content":"Step numbers (`\"N. \"`) are prepended automatically — keep them where possible, as user testing shows people recognize the component better with them. Set `hideStepNumbers` to omit them."},"798":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-31","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#customization","content":"`orientation` switches between `horizontal` (accent bar on top) and `vertical` (accent bar on the leading edge)."},"799":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-32","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#customization","content":"`currentStep` is the single source of truth for the timeline. Omit it for a not-yet-started flow where every step is `future`; pass the step count for a fully completed flow where every step is `past`."},"800":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-33","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#customization","content":"`status` is independent of timeline and only controls the status icon and (for `error`) the accent bar color."},"801":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-34","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#customization","content":"Pass `className` to the container or an individual step to extend the styles."},"802":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-35","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#accessibility","content":"The container renders a `<nav>` landmark; set `aria-label` to name it (defaults to `\"Progress\"`)."},"803":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-36","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#accessibility","content":"Steps are an ordered list (`<ol>`/`<li>`) so assistive technology conveys position and count."},"804":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-37","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#accessibility","content":"The current step is marked with `aria-current=\"step\"`."},"805":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-38","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#accessibility","content":"Interactive steps are real buttons: focusable in the natural **Tab** order and activated with **Enter** or **Space**. Status icons are decorative (`aria-hidden`)."},"806":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-39","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#accessibility","content":"Focus is shown with a visible outline; disabled steps use `0.4` opacity and are not focusable."},"807":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-40","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#best-practices","content":"Drive the timeline from `currentStep` rather than styling individual steps."},"808":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-41","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#best-practices","content":"Provide `onPress` only for steps a user can actually navigate to; leave it off for display-only steps."},"809":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-42","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#best-practices","content":"Keep titles short — they truncate with an ellipsis when space is tight."},"810":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-43","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#best-practices","content":"Always give the container an `aria-label` that describes the flow (e.g. `\"Checkout progress\"`)."},"811":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-44","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#troubleshooting","content":"**No step is highlighted:** `currentStep` is omitted, negative, or out of range. Set it to the active step's 0-based index."},"812":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-45","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#troubleshooting","content":"**A step isn't clickable:** it has no `onPress`, so it's inert by design. Add `onPress` to make it interactive."},"813":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-46","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#troubleshooting","content":"**Titles overflow:** that's expected — titles truncate. Shorten the title."},"814":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"page","content":"RangeField","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field"},"815":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-0","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field","content":"RangeField lets users select one or multiple independently adjustable numeric values on a shared bounded scale."},"816":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-1","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#features","content":"Features"},"817":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-2","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#installation","content":"Installation"},"818":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-3","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#props","content":"Props"},"819":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-4","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#examples","content":"Examples"},"820":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-5","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#default","content":"Default"},"821":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-6","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#controlled","content":"Controlled"},"822":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-7","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#disabled","content":"Disabled"},"823":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-8","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#labels","content":"Labels"},"824":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-9","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#markers","content":"Markers"},"825":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-10","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#range","content":"Range"},"826":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-11","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#customization","content":"Customization"},"827":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-12","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#value-shape-and-thumbs","content":"Value shape and thumbs"},"828":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-13","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#programmatic-focus","content":"Programmatic focus"},"829":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-14","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#value-display","content":"Value display"},"830":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-15","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#endpoint-labels-and-markers","content":"Endpoint labels and markers"},"831":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-16","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#number-formatting","content":"Number formatting"},"832":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-17","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#visual-styling","content":"Visual styling"},"833":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-18","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"834":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-19","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"Accessible names"},"835":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-20","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Keyboard interaction"},"836":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-21","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#value-announcements","content":"Value announcements"},"837":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-22","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#instructions-required-state-and-errors","content":"Instructions, required state, and errors"},"838":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-23","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#disabled-state","content":"Disabled state"},"839":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-24","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"840":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-25","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"841":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-26","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#a-thumb-is-missing-a-label-or-form-value","content":"A thumb is missing a label or form value"},"842":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-27","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#typescript-reports-the-wrong-callback-value-type","content":"TypeScript reports the wrong callback value type"},"843":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-28","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-controlled-thumbs-do-not-move","content":"The controlled thumbs do not move"},"844":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-29","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-wrong-thumb-changes-meaning","content":"The wrong thumb changes meaning"},"845":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-30","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#values-snap-unexpectedly","content":"Values snap unexpectedly"},"846":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-31","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-final-marker-is-missing","content":"The final marker is missing"},"847":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-32","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#markers-are-crowded-or-rendering-is-slow","content":"Markers are crowded or rendering is slow"},"848":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-33","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-value-or-endpoint-labels-are-blank","content":"The value or endpoint labels are blank"},"849":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-34","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#negative-values-do-not-behave-as-expected","content":"Negative values do not behave as expected"},"850":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-35","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-range-configuration-is-invalid","content":"The range configuration is invalid"},"851":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-36","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#features","content":"Generic `number` or `number[]` value with one thumb for each array entry"},"852":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-37","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#features","content":"Type-aligned controlled and uncontrolled state, including `onChange` and `onChangeEnd`"},"853":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-38","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#features","content":"Per-thumb accessible labels and native form names matched by array index"},"854":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-39","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#features","content":"Configurable minimum, maximum, and step values, including negative numeric ranges"},"855":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-40","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#features","content":"Optional localized value output, endpoint labels, description, error message, and markers"},"856":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-41","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#features","content":"Required, disabled, keyboard, pointer, and touch behavior provided through React Aria"},"857":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-42","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#props","content":"`RangeField` infers its generic value type from `value` or `defaultValue`, keeping `onChange` and `onChangeEnd` aligned with either `number` or `number[]`. Provide the generic explicitly when inference is not available, for example `<RangeField<number[]> />`."},"858":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-43","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#default","content":"Use the default presentation for one adjustable value on a continuous track."},"859":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-44","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#controlled","content":"Use `onChange` for immediate updates and `onChangeEnd` for work that should run after interaction finishes."},"860":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-45","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#disabled","content":"Use `isDisabled` when the value is visible but unavailable for interaction."},"861":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-46","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#labels","content":"Combine an input label, value label, range labels, and helper text when users need additional context."},"862":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-47","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#markers","content":"Use markers to expose a manageable set of discrete steps for a single value."},"863":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-48","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#range","content":"Pass two values to render a range with two thumbs and step markers."},"864":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-49","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#customization","content":"`RangeField` supports scalar and array values, so customize it according to the number and meaning of the rendered thumbs. Prefer its content props and CSS custom properties over targeting the internal DOM structure."},"865":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-50","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#value-shape-and-thumbs","content":"A `number` renders one thumb. A `number[]` renders one thumb per array entry. The generic type keeps `value`, `defaultValue`, `onChange`, and `onChangeEnd` aligned:"},"866":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-51","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#value-shape-and-thumbs","content":"TypeScript usually infers the type from `value` or `defaultValue`. Supply `<number>` or `<number[]>` explicitly when the initial props do not provide enough information for inference."},"867":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-52","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#programmatic-focus","content":"Attach a `RangeFieldRef` when an application needs to move focus after validation or navigate to the field. Calling `focus()` focuses the first thumb; `container` exposes the root element for DOM operations such as scrolling."},"868":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-53","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#value-display","content":"Use `valueLabel` to place content opposite the field label:"},"869":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-54","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#value-display","content":"`true` displays all current values using `formatOptions` and the active locale."},"870":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-55","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#value-display","content":"A React node displays static content."},"871":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-56","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#value-display","content":"A render function receives the React Aria slider state and can derive output from every current value."},"872":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-57","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#value-display","content":"`valueLabel` is visual supporting content. It does not name the field or its individual thumbs."},"873":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-58","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#endpoint-labels-and-markers","content":"`minLabel` and `maxLabel` are independent `ReactNode` slots below the track. Provide either one or both; the component does not generate or format their content. Each slot uses at most 40% of the available width so the sides remain visually separated."},"874":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-59","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#endpoint-labels-and-markers","content":"Set `markers` to render one marker for every valid step beginning at `minValue`. Marker positions use the same scale as every thumb. `minValue`, `maxValue`, and `step` determine their count and spacing; `markers` does not accept a custom list or count."},"875":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-60","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#number-formatting","content":"`formatOptions` accepts `Intl.NumberFormatOptions` and controls localized output for the default value label and assistive-technology announcements. It does not format `minLabel` or `maxLabel` because those props accept arbitrary React content."},"876":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-61","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#visual-styling","content":"Pass `className` to add a class to the root element. The following custom properties are the supported styling surface:"},"877":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-62","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#visual-styling","content":"`--slider-track-height`"},"878":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-63","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#visual-styling","content":"`--slider-fill-height`"},"879":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-64","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#visual-styling","content":"`--slider-thumb-size`"},"880":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-65","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#visual-styling","content":"`--slider-marker-size`"},"881":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-66","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#visual-styling","content":"`--slider-fill-color`"},"882":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-67","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#visual-styling","content":"`--slider-track-color`"},"883":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-68","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#visual-styling","content":"`--slider-thumb-bg`"},"884":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-69","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#visual-styling","content":"`--slider-thumb-border`"},"885":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-70","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#visual-styling","content":"`--slider-label-color`"},"886":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-71","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#visual-styling","content":"Scope overrides to a local class so other range fields are unaffected."},"887":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-72","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"Every range field needs a name as a whole. Prefer a visible `label`; use `aria-label` only when equivalent visible context already exists."},"888":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-73","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"When using an array, provide one descriptive `thumbLabels` entry for every value. Entries are matched by index, so the labels must remain aligned when values are added, removed, or reordered. Describe each thumb's purpose, such as `Lower warning threshold`, rather than its current number."},"889":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-74","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"`thumbNames` configures native form field names and does not provide accessible labels. Likewise, `valueLabel`, `minLabel`, and `maxLabel` are visual context rather than substitutes for accessible naming."},"890":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-75","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Each thumb follows the React Aria slider keyboard model:"},"891":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-76","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Tab and Shift+Tab move among thumbs and surrounding controls."},"892":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-77","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Arrow Right and Arrow Up increase the focused value by `step`."},"893":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-78","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Arrow Left and Arrow Down decrease the focused value by `step`."},"894":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-79","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Home and End move the focused thumb to its permitted bounds."},"895":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-80","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Page Up and Page Down make larger changes."},"896":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-81","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Directional behavior follows the user's locale where appropriate. Pointer, touch, and keyboard interaction all use the same scale and constraints."},"897":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-82","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#value-announcements","content":"Use `formatOptions` to expose the meaning and unit of each number to assistive technology. A percentage, currency, or measurement should be announced in that format rather than as an unexplained raw value."},"898":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-83","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#value-announcements","content":"Markers are decorative and hidden from the accessibility tree. Ensure the field label, thumb labels, bounds, step, and formatted values communicate all required information without relying on marker appearance."},"899":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-84","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#instructions-required-state-and-errors","content":"Use `description` for persistent guidance that applies to every thumb. Set `isRequired` when the field is required, and use `errorMessage` with the component's validation state to explain how to correct an invalid selection. React Aria associates this content with the control; write errors that identify both the affected value and the corrective action when multiple thumbs are present."},"900":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-85","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#disabled-state","content":"`isDisabled` prevents interaction with every thumb and exposes the disabled state semantically. The slider control is visually muted while the label, endpoint labels, description, and error text remain readable."},"901":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-86","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use a scalar value for one adjustable number and an array only when each entry has a clear, independently adjustable meaning."},"902":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-87","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Keep `value`, `thumbLabels`, and `thumbNames` aligned by index. Treat them as parallel collections whenever values are added, removed, or reordered."},"903":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-88","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use thumb labels that explain purpose instead of repeating the current number."},"904":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-89","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Keep array values in a stable semantic order. If crossing or reordering thumbs would make their meaning ambiguous, enforce the appropriate ordering in product state."},"905":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-90","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Avoid large value arrays. Every entry creates another focusable control, which increases keyboard effort and cognitive load."},"906":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-91","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Set meaningful `minValue`, `maxValue`, and `step` values. The scale should match the precision users actually need."},"907":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-92","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use markers only when there are few enough steps to scan. Tiny steps across a large range can create an excessive number of DOM elements."},"908":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-93","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `formatOptions` for currency, percentages, measurements, and other locale-sensitive units."},"909":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-94","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `onChange` for lightweight immediate feedback and `onChangeEnd` for expensive requests, filtering, or calculations."},"910":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-95","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use a text-entry control when exact numeric input is essential. A track is best for exploring or adjusting values within known bounds."},"911":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-96","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#a-thumb-is-missing-a-label-or-form-value","content":"Check the same index in `thumbLabels` and `thumbNames`. Each array entry renders a thumb, and its accessible label and form name are read from the corresponding positions. A form name does not replace an accessible label."},"912":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-97","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#typescript-reports-the-wrong-callback-value-type","content":"Keep the controlled or default value and callback signatures consistent. When inference is unavailable, provide the generic explicitly: `<RangeField<number>>` for a scalar or `<RangeField<number[]>>` for an array."},"913":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-98","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-controlled-thumbs-do-not-move","content":"The `value` prop is the source of truth. Update the scalar or array in `onChange` without changing its intended shape. For arrays, return a new array so application state observes the update."},"914":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-99","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-wrong-thumb-changes-meaning","content":"Values, `thumbLabels`, and `thumbNames` are associated by index. Update all parallel arrays together and keep their semantic order stable."},"915":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-100","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#values-snap-unexpectedly","content":"Verify that `step` represents the intended interval from `minValue`. Every thumb snaps to valid positions on the same configured scale."},"916":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-101","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-final-marker-is-missing","content":"Markers begin at `minValue` and appear at complete step positions. `maxValue` receives a marker only when the range is evenly divisible by `step`."},"917":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-102","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#markers-are-crowded-or-rendering-is-slow","content":"Increase `step` or omit `markers`. Large ranges with small steps can produce many decorative elements even when users cannot distinguish them visually."},"918":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-103","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-value-or-endpoint-labels-are-blank","content":"Enable automatic current-value output with `valueLabel={true}` or provide custom content. `minLabel` and `maxLabel` display only explicitly supplied content; neither defaults to a numeric bound or receives `formatOptions`."},"919":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-104","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#negative-values-do-not-behave-as-expected","content":"Negative values are supported. Set a negative `minValue` and ensure every scalar or array value remains within the configured bounds."},"920":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-105","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-range-configuration-is-invalid","content":"Provide finite bounds where `minValue` is less than `maxValue`, a finite `step` greater than zero, and finite values inside the configured range."},"921":{"id":"/docs/components/radio","page_id":"/docs/components/radio","type":"page","content":"Radio","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/radio"},"922":{"id":"/docs/components/radio-0","page_id":"/docs/components/radio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/radio","content":"Accessible radio button component for mutually exclusive selections with keyboard navigation, validation states, and flexible layouts."},"923":{"id":"/docs/components/radio-1","page_id":"/docs/components/radio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/radio#instal